for defense as it stops Black from forming a dangerous Open 3 along the I7-H8 diagonal. Additionally, G9 creates a constructive shape for White by connecting diagonally with H10, offering a balance of defense and potential counter-attack.\n\nReason: Black threatens to create an Open 3 at either G9 or K9. White must block one of these to prevent Black from gaining a winning momentum. G9 is preferred over K9 because it simultaneously blocks the threat and connects with White\'s stone at H10, creating a stronger defensive structure.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "G", "row": 9}'}
